.\" ar.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX ar(1) utility, which this tree
.\" does not provide. An original page (this project's own text), so
.\" it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code, same
.\" posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec 5
.\" ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-litigated.
.\" Rendered at build time to build/man/AR.TXT and staged on the
.\" play image as /usr/man/AR.
.TH AR 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
ar \- create and maintain library archives
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ar
is not provided on maux.
ld(1) links object modules from library DIRECTORIES (/LIB/LIBK,
given to the linker as -l k), not from archive files, so there
is no archive format for ar to manage.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ld(1)
